From 30c7cba21b3a5dfbba6f055a003e3a3726f36340 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:08:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/57] hw/misc, hw/char: review fixes for migration, logging
 and WDT

- Clock models migrate every clock: the GCLK source inputs and the
  outputs of OSCCTRL, OSC32KCTRL, GCLK and MCLK. Before, the outputs came
  back at their reset rates after loadvm, and the next GCLK write
  propagated a wrong CPU clock (48 MHz -> 2 MHz instead of 24 MHz).
- SERCOM: pre_load drops a pending chardev watch; post_load rejects an
  impossible rx_count and defers the TX retry and accept_input to a
  virtual-clock timer, so nothing happens before every device is loaded
  and the VM runs; finalize removes the watch.
- Generic register blocks log at most 8 unmodelled writes per register,
  then "further writes not logged".
- NVIC: ICSR.RETTOBASE reads as zero on ARMv6-M (reserved there).
- WDT CONFIG and EWCTRL are enable-protected (also while ALWAYSON);
  regenerated wdt_u2251.h. New qtest pic32cm-jh/wdt-protection.

Peripheral Pretender downstream patch; not for upstream submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
